From: CarPlay C0 lane (2026-11-22)
Subject: 0516 sweet_nub: sample again after the direct createUSBDevice call

0512's sample runs five seconds after registerService, i.e. BEFORE 0513's direct fallback, so it
cannot report what the fallback built. Three seconds after the direct call the probe now prints
whether the controller became active, its retain count, and its IOService-plane children with
class names. Those children are the IOUSBDeviceInterface objects createUSBDevice constructs; if
they appear, S5 is answered on the device instead of being inferred from silence.

Prepared while the phone was off-USB (2026-11-22 02:24 hang, other lane's boot). Dispatch is held
until the S02/S3d/S3ibd boots show whether the configurator or the fallback path is the one that
runs, so this only ships if it is actually needed.

--- a/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
@@ -312,6 +312,28 @@
 				uint32_t ir = ((uint32_t (*)(IOService *, OSDictionary *))
 				    SWEET_NUB_CREATE_USBDEVICE)(ctl, desc);
 				printf("SWEET NUB: direct createUSBDevice -> 0x%08x\n", ir);
+				/*
+				 * 0516: the 5 s sample ran BEFORE this call, so it cannot show what the call
+				 * built. Sample again three seconds later: interfaces created by Apple's
+				 * createUSBDevice are children in the IOService plane, and a started controller
+				 * flips isInactive() to false.
+				 */
+				(void)tsleep(&sweet_nub_wait, PZERO, "sweetnub3", 3 * hz);
+				printf("SWEET NUB: after direct call: started %d, retain %d\n",
+				    ctl->isInactive() ? 0 : 1, ctl->getRetainCount());
+				auto made_it = ctl->getChildIterator(gIOServicePlane);
+				int made = 0;
+				if (made_it) {
+					while (OSObject *obj = made_it->getNextObject()) {
+						IOService *child = OSDynamicCast(IOService, obj);
+						if (child != NULL) {
+							printf("SWEET NUB: made[%d] %s\n", made,
+							    child->getMetaClass()->getClassName());
+						}
+						made++;
+					}
+				}
+				printf("SWEET NUB: after direct call: children %d\n", made);
 			} else {
 				printf("SWEET NUB: cannot allocate the description values\n");
 			}
